Modifications in this fork (the "pro" enhanced edition) include:
  - A Codex-style reasoning-effort slider popover beside the composer model
    trigger: named tiers with a per-tier signature palette, magnetic detents,
    a damped glide (170 ms) while dragging, a Max-flow treatment at the top
    tier, animated tick/sheen feedback, a live value readout, full ARIA slider
    semantics, keyboard control, and a prefers-reduced-motion path.
  - A dark/light theme token pass for the picker and effort popover, including
    a light-scheme contrast pass for tier ink, tracks, ticks, and hints.
  - Design-only polish: roomier rows, a unified type ladder, token-based hover
    and press feedback, and narrow-screen fallbacks (ends-only effort scale
    under 520 px; full-width bottom sheet on phones). No business logic changed.
  - An opt-in host-composer restyle (composerRestyle, default OFF), shipped in a
    separate stylesheet the client mounts only when the user enables it, because
    its selectors are host-global.
  - Renamed package/plugin identity to dsh-model-switcher-pro (the upstream npm
    name dsh-model-switcher is already published by the upstream author). The
    browser localStorage key (dsh-model-switcher:v1) and the locale dictionary
    namespace (model-switcher) are kept stable so existing user history survives.

The base picker behavior, keyboard model, enrichment reads, and the modelSwitcher
client service are carried over from upstream. Provider marks are generated from
simple-icons (https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons), CC0-1.0; the brands
belong to their respective owners.